ntestable** when a careful, reasonable colleague could still argue that it meets the request (for\n  example, \"the Pricing sheet file\" when the record is \"Pricing sheet 2025.xlsx\"). Say so for that record; it is\n  not the same as failing nothing.\n\nBe precise. Judge each condition on its own; do not let one record's overall fit sway you. When a condition turns on\na time, compute it in the stated time zone. When it turns on a person, match the exact person.\n\n\n---\n\nA user of Slack gave an assistant this request:\n\n> Add a check reaction to the 2.4 rollout message in #releases that lena.hart@northwind.example has already reacted with 👀 to — the one a human posted, not the bot's.\n\nThe person making the request is the workspace's assistant bot (U01AGENBOT9), acting for the team.\n\nStep 1: list the conditions a record must meet for this request to refer to it, and every phrase that could reasonably be read in more than one way.","run_stream":{"id":"e71364e9-d8ba-40f2-8701-178542f22ade","kind":"run"}}}
